  <div id="sutta">
  
          <h4 id="thig2.3" class="h1">Thig 2:3  Sumaṅgala’s Mother</h4>
          <div class="verse">
            <p>So freed! So freed!</p>
            <p>So thoroughly freed am I—</p>
            <p class="v2">from my pestle,</p>
            <p class="v2">my shameless husband</p>
            <p class="v2">&amp; his sun-shade making,</p>
            <p class="v2">my moldy old pot</p>
            <p class="v2">with its water-snake smell.</p>
            <p>Aversion &amp; passion</p>
            <p>I cut with a <em>chop.</em></p>
            <p>Having come to the foot of a tree,</p>
            <p>I do jhāna, from the bliss thinking:</p>
            <p class="v2">“What bliss!”</p>
          </div><!--end verse-->
          <p class="seealso">See also: <a href="../Thag/thag1_43.html">Thag 1:43</a></p><!--end seealso-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
